# Mutation plan for the SAML, LDAP and audit-log certificate and enterprise-gate routes
# (`mm_api::auth_certs`, `mm_api::local_auth_certs`, `mm_app::auth_certs`).
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/auth-certs.plan
#
# Every line is a decision a reader could get wrong and that `parity::auth_certs` has a row to
# catch: which filename each `HasFile` reads (the public certificate is installed when the status
# is compared, so a swap reads a different answer), the count predicate behind it, the licence
# gate and its order against the permission on `sync` (plain user, unlicensed: 501 not 403) and
# on `migrateid` (403 not 501), the empty checks on `toAttribute` and `saml_metadata_url`, the
# `null` refusal of `reset_auth_data`, the two halves of the auth-service rule, the PEM media
# type and the missing-type branch of the idp add, the audit parser's two-part refusal, the LDAP
# parser's id, and the third diagnostic test name. Two no-op controls close the plan.

status-public-reads-private	crates/mm-app/src/auth_certs.rs	.has_config_file(saml.public_certificate_file.as_deref())	.has_config_file(saml.private_key_file.as_deref())	api	auth_certs
